- op: discuss  # 256b
  at: '2026-09-06T12:25:47Z'  # 256b
  by: agent  # 256b
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 256b
  clock: 4  # 256b
  nonce: 256b  # 256b
  message: "SCOPED 2026-09-06, read-only, before any fix (LIVE rule 20: pre-register, then measure).\n\nTHE MECHANISM, exactly. linkers/solidity_abi.py:206-232 mints, per JS/TS call site, a Symbol with id `typescript:{rel_path}:{line}-{line}:abi_call:{func}:{hash}` -- the language SLOT of the id is the literal \"typescript\" -- while the Symbol itself carries `language=None, discovery_language=\"typescript\", protocol_origin=\"solidity_abi\"` (ADR-0031 Class B: \"Was LITERAL-HOST\"). So the node's language field is None (it is not counted under any language in the survey's node census: openzeppelin shows 0 typescript nodes) but the EDGE's src id says typescript, and compute_boundary_coverage (verify_claims.py ~3628-3648) derives languages_with_calls from `src.split(\":\", 1)[0]`. Two readers of one identifier disagree, and the gate reads the one the linker never meant as a language claim.\n\nSIBLINGS BY MECHANISM (LIVE rule 4): linkers/tauri_ipc.py:638, :766, :870 mint `f\"typescript:{rel_path}...\"` / `f\"typescript:{ts_path}...\"` ids the same way; crypto_flow.py:283-284 and message_dispatch.py:258-259 use `f\"{lang}:...\"` with a real language variable (not a sibling); js_module.py:243 `f\"{lang}:npm:0-0:{name}:package\"` likewise. WI-mital's build_target case was the manifest pseudo-language; this is the second linker family found by the same rung.\n\nFIX SHAPE, two layers, both needed:\n  1. AT THE LINKER: the id's language slot is the HOST FILE's language (javascript for .js, typescript for .ts) -- the call site really is in that file -- and the Symbol's `language` should say the same rather than None, so node census and edge prefix agree. Check tauri_ipc the same way.\n  2. AT THE GATE, the general guard WI-mital's docstring already argues for: identify a synthetic src by what MINTED it (origin), never by its language. is_synthetic_build_target_call is one linker's predicate; the shared form is \"a call edge whose origin is a linker that mints synthetic call-site srcs, or whose src is not a node the analyzers produced, does not add its language to languages_with_calls\". Without (2), the next linker with a literal repeats this.\n\nMEASURE: openzeppelin-contracts NO-NET before/after (6689 typescript-prefixed call edges; the verdict should move off this rung to the next one that holds it -- solidity has no catalogue, so it stays inconclusive naming solidity alone), plus any tauri repo in the corpus for the sibling. The read-back is the reason string, not the category."  # 256b
