- op: discuss  # fddf
  at: '2026-09-06T13:03:05Z'  # fddf
  by: agent  # fddf
  actor: jgstern_agent  # fddf
  clock: 6  # fddf
  nonce: fddf  # fddf
  message: "DONE 2026-09-06 (PR #798), layer 1 of the scoping entry above, widened from two emitters to six by the sweep. Symbol.language stays None (Class B) everywhere; the id's language slot and discovery_language are the host file's (js_ts_language_from_path). Pinned per extension with .ts controls in test_solidity_abi_linker.py, test_tauri_ipc_linker.py, test_message_dispatch_linker.py, test_crypto_flow_linker.py, test_yjs_crdt_linker.py, test_wasm_bindgen_linker.py, test_grpc_linker.py.\n\nBEHAVIOURAL EVIDENCE, the item's own instance, openzeppelin-contracts through the production CLI on a cleared cache (~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/dovog_abi_src_09062026/after/):\n  BEFORE (js-leg new arm, same catalogues): NO-NET inconclusive | \"language(s) solidity, typescript made calls but have no I/O catalog\"; survey: 6689 typescript-prefixed calls edges (solidity-abi-linker) + 38 typescript-prefixed event_publishes edges (message-dispatch-linker), 0 typescript nodes.\n  AFTER (abi + tauri + message_dispatch + crypto_flow fixed; the later yjs/wasm/grpc fixes touch no openzeppelin edge): NO-NET inconclusive | \"language(s) solidity made calls but have no I/O catalog\"; survey: 0 typescript-prefixed edges of ANY type. NO-FSWRITE/NO-FSREAD/NO-SUBPROC violated 14/19/6 in both arms.\n  The verdict category does not move -- solidity has no catalogue and holds the rung next -- and that is the honest read-back: this fix removes a FALSE reason, not a true withholding.\n\nTHE FAMILY, swept by mechanism (LIVE rule 4) and each pinned per extension: solidity_abi.py (1 site), tauri_ipc.py (publisher, caller, event-listener), message_dispatch.py and crypto_flow.py (a conditional literal from the WRITE site's api kind, which also gave a .ts read site the write's language), yjs_crdt.py (pub/sub), wasm_bindgen.py (TS-side import stand-in), grpc.py (_scan_ts_file's client-pattern language). Six linkers, all now js_ts_language_from_path.\nNo tauri repository exists in the corpus (find over the four corpus roots: no tauri.conf.json), so the tauri sibling is pinned by its tests only.\n\nRESIDUAL, layer 2, not built: compute_boundary_coverage still derives \"a language made calls\" from the src id's first segment. The shared guard WI-mital's docstring argues for -- identify a synthetic src by its ORIGIN (or by the absence of an analyzer-produced node), never by its language -- would stop the next linker with a literal from repeating this. Filed as the open half of this item; INV-kurup (identifier-bearing fields from several emission paths) carries the META pointer."  # fddf
